%% Lifecycle of an authenticated REST request (backend/api/middleware.py, deps.py, routes_*.py)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client (web / mobile)
    participant CORS as CORSMiddleware
    participant RID as RequestCorrelationMiddleware
    participant R as Router handler
    participant D as Dependencies (get_db, get_current_user / require_*)
    participant DB as Database
    participant EH as Exception handlers

    C->>CORS: GET /api/v1/decisions/latest (Authorization: Bearer JWT)
    CORS->>RID: pass (adds CORS headers on the way out)
    RID->>RID: request_id = X-Request-ID or uuid4
    RID->>R: route match
    R->>D: resolve dependencies
    D->>DB: open AsyncSession
    D->>D: decode JWT (HS256), check exp
    D->>DB: load user, check is_active and token_version
    D->>D: role check (403 if not allowed)
    R->>DB: query via repository / select()
    DB-->>R: rows
    R-->>RID: Pydantic response model -> JSON
    RID-->>C: 200 + X-Request-ID
    Note over R,EH: Any HTTPException / validation error / unhandled error<br/>is converted to {"error": {code, message, request_id, details}}
    R--xEH: raise HTTPException
    EH-->>C: 4xx/5xx error envelope
